(395789, 32396, 5222, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by amsmyth:</b></div><hr/><i>desolation...but is that a thermos?</i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>No it was a can of beer. "His only friend", I walked straight passed this guy that morning, when I turned around I felt really sad but wanted to photograph him.</td>', 'Originally posted by amsmyth:desolation...but is that a thermos?  No it was a can of beer. "His only friend", I walked straight passed this guy that morning, when I turned around I felt really sad but wanted to photograph him.', '2003-08-22 09:09:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(395792, 32396, 5222, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Pidd:</b></div><hr/><i>This is a good interpretation of the theme but perhaps just a little too dark on your subject.  I think that seeing the folds of the coat (and maybe the tatters if they are there) would create even more empathy for this pour soul.  Your title evokes quite a bit of emotion.</i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thanks for the comment. <br/><a href="//www.geocities.com/espenyogi888/photo.htm" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">This is my photo gallery</a></td>', 'Originally posted by Pidd:This is a good interpretation of the theme but perhaps just a little too dark on your subject.  I think that seeing the folds of the coat (and maybe the tatters if they are there) would create even more empathy for this pour soul.  Your title evokes quite a bit of emotion.  Thanks for the comment. This is my photo gallery', '2003-08-22 09:13:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(395809, 32396, 5222, '<td valign="top">Thank you everyone for your comments! I felt really bad taking this picture without asking and wanted to give him some change for been such a still photographic model. He was sleeping though and I didn''t want to wake him up.<br/> <br/>P.S: I try and write crediting and critic comments whenever I view other peoples photos and like to get the same response back. (e.g; Pidd''s comment about been too dark) it''s sometimes hard to do this given the amount of photographs in the competitions but it''s the only way I focus on taking a better shots and become a better photographer. I try and do my best and give the same out to other people as well.<br/> <br/>(Sorry about that. It''s just something I had on my shoulders after a DP user got really upset because I said that you should try and think about the shot before taking it). "A photo that just looked like a quick snap shot and entered into the last contest".</td>', 'Thank you everyone for your comments! I felt really bad taking this picture without asking and wanted to give him some change for been such a still photographic model. He was sleeping though and I didn''t want to wake him up. P.S: I try and write crediting and critic comments whenever I view other peoples photos and like to get the same response back. (e.g; Pidd''s comment about been too dark) it''s sometimes hard to do this given the amount of photographs in the competitions but it''s the only way I focus on taking a better shots and become a better photographer. I try and do my best and give the same out to other people as well. (Sorry about that. It''s just something I had on my shoulders after a DP user got really upset because I said that you should try and think about the shot before taking it). "A photo that just looked like a quick snap shot and entered into the last contest".', '2003-08-22 09:27:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(395811, 32989, 5222, '<td valign="top">well done on the result and thanks for your reply. <br/><a href="//www.geocities.com/espenyogi888/photo.htm" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">My photo Gallery</a></td>', 'well done on the result and thanks for your reply. My photo Gallery', '2003-08-22 09:31:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(395998, 32813, 11111, '<td valign="top">OK, here you go. I liked this one quite a bit though the girl''s outfit and ponytails make her too cheery for the topic. Great job capturing natural color - the girl''s shirt, brick, peeling paint, wall. I also like the textures - metal, wood, brick. The cropping seems a little tight at top and at right, to me. What I like most about this is the "layered" effect that draws my eye through the doorway, into the room, and through the window to the boards. You''ve captured a lot here without it being too busy or distracting. Hope this helps. I''m no pro.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2003-08-22 10:41:30.</i></td>', 'OK, here you go. I liked this one quite a bit though the girl''s outfit and ponytails make her too cheery for the topic. Great job capturing natural color - the girl''s shirt, brick, peeling paint, wall. I also like the textures - metal, wood, brick. The cropping seems a little tight at top and at right, to me. What I like most about this is the "layered" effect that draws my eye through the doorway, into the room, and through the window to the boards. You''ve captured a lot here without it being too busy or distracting. Hope this helps. I''m no pro.', '2003-08-22 11:40:47.000000', '2003-08-22 11:41:30.000000', 0),
(396324, 33045, 8829, '<td valign="top">Who in the world would only give this shot a 2?! Talk about unrealistic standards...jeez. Even on a bad day this should get nothing less than a 6...Great shot.</td>', 'Who in the world would only give this shot a 2?! Talk about unrealistic standards...jeez. Even on a bad day this should get nothing less than a 6...Great shot.', '2003-08-22 15:33:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(396555, 32407, 1135, '<td valign="top">I got it, and gave it a 7. Very much implies Desolation to me not to mention that it was a difficult shot to expose correctly. Should have been much higher in the list IMHO.</td>', 'I got it, and gave it a 7. Very much implies Desolation to me not to mention that it was a difficult shot to expose correctly. Should have been much higher in the list IMHO.', '2003-08-22 18:43:10.000000', NULL, 0),
